@host = http://localhost:5199

### Log in. Other seeded users: admin@, manager@, leader@, member1@, member2@ (all @mizan.local)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "client@mizan.local",
  "password": "Mizan@123"
}

### Current user, using the token from the login above
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Wrong password: expect 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "client@mizan.local",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### No token: expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### Create a ticket: expect 201 as a client, 403 as anyone else
# @name createTicket
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Fix the null reference on checkout",
  "description": "The checkout page crashes when the cart is empty.",
  "repositoryUrl": "https://github.com/demo-client/shop-api",
  "branch": "main",
  "commitSha": "a1b2c3d",
  "priority": "High"
}

### Bad input: expect 400 with an errors field
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad ticket",
  "description": "Every marked field is invalid.",
  "repositoryUrl": "https://example.com/not-github",
  "branch": "main",
  "commitSha": "not-a-sha",
  "priority": 99
}

### Tickets the logged-in user can see
GET {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Ticket details: expect 200, or 404 if this user can't see it
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Unknown ticket: expect 404
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Ticket history (audit log). Clients see only the public steps.
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

########## Workflow ##########
# Log in as the right user for each step (change the email in the login request above):
#   route / reject                  -> manager@
#   assign, leader-approve/send-back -> leader@
#   submit                          -> member1@ (after being assigned)
#   manager-approve/send-back       -> manager@ (the one who routed it)
#   close / reopen                  -> client@
# Every step returns the updated ticket; "allowedActions" shows what this user can do next.

### Teams (manager: all teams, leader: their own). Use an id from here for "route".
# @name teams
GET {{host}}/api/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Route to a team (manager)
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/route
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": "{{teams.response.body.$[0].id}}" }

### Reject (manager, only while Submitted)
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Assign members (leader of the ticket's team). Member ids come from GET /api/teams.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberIds": ["{{teams.response.body.$[0].members[0].id}}"] }

### Submit the fix (assigned member)
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "branch": "fix/checkout",
  "commitSha": "b2c3d4e",
  "summary": "Added a null check for an empty cart."
}

### Leader approves / sends back
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/leader-approve
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/leader-send-back
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Manager approves (sends the response to the client) / sends back
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/manager-approve
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/manager-send-back
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Client closes / reopens
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/{{createTicket.response.body.$.id}}/reopen
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
